@inject NavigationManager Navigation

@* Renders nothing. It stands in for the refusal page when the refusal is "you have not enrolled a
   second factor yet", and sends the session to the one place it can do something about that.

   Signing in already lands there: all three sign-in paths answer RequiresMfaEnrollment with
   /account/security?setup=required. Being GRANTED an MFA-required role mid-session reaches the same
   state by a different road - the principal refreshes, the claims factory stamps MfaSetupPending, and
   every gate starts refusing - but nothing was routing it anywhere, so a promotion read as the app
   breaking rather than as a step to take. Same state, same destination.

   The refusal itself is not what moves: the gates go on refusing regardless (see MfaEnrollmentGuard).
   This only decides what the person sees while they are refused. *@

@code {
    protected override void OnAfterRender(bool firstRender)
    {
        // After the first interactive render rather than in OnInitialized: this component is reached
        // through the router's NotAuthorized fragment, which prerenders, and a redirect issued from
        // there races the circuit it is about to replace.
        if (firstRender)
            Navigation.NavigateTo("/account/security?setup=required", forceLoad: false, replace: true);
    }
}
